From 21240f6b622c0ac19a2ce4f267533b5d767b6c7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Redesign <redesign@local>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 02:52:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Redesign: brand palette, readable type, structured resource
 pages

Visual and structural pass over the Seniors for Climate BC site.

Fixes carried over from the upstream coffee-shop template:
- html had background-color: var(--black), putting a black backdrop
  behind every page
- p had a global max-width of 32rem inside 48rem containers, so
  paragraphs stopped short of their own headings
- root font-size ramped 18/20/22px, making Tachyons' f1 render at 66px
- --grey-3 was #9B9B9B: 2.8:1 on white, failing WCAG AA on the hero
  subhead and all card text
- the footer set #385080 headings on pure black, roughly 2.4:1
- the mobile hamburger had markup and CSS but no JS ever toggled
  .menu-open, so tapping it did nothing
- mask-icon and theme-color were still the template's #ff4400

Palette now comes from the logo artwork (green #4E7A1E wordmark, blue
#0D6591 illustration). The previous --primary navy #385080 appears in
no brand asset; see OPEN QUESTIONS in the content deliverable.

Resource pages moved from markdown link lists into front matter, so
title / publisher / date / format / description are separate fields
rather than one string joined by em dashes. Rendered by
partials/resources.html. All 65 URLs verified byte-identical to the
originals, including the Sierra Club mkt_tok parameter and every
Google Drive link.

Type is Source Serif 4 for headings and resource titles, Public Sans
for body, at a flat 20px base.
